            "result_text": "Done! I've created the `run_tasks` function in `/app/run.py`. Here's how it works:\n\n- **Semaphore limiting**: Uses `asyncio.Semaphore(max_concurrent)` to ensure at most `max_concurrent` tasks run at the same time\n- **Cleanup on interruption**: When you press Ctrl+C, asyncio will cancel pending tasks, and any `try/finally` blocks or async context managers in your tasks will execute their cleanup code before the interrupt propagates\n- **return_exceptions=True**: Ensures if one task fails, others continue running (and their cleanup code still runs)\n\nYou can import and use it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        # do work\n    finally:\n        # cleanup happens here even on Ctrl+C\n        pass\n\nawait run_tasks([my_task, my_task, ...], max_concurrent=3)\n```"
